---
/*
 * A storage move while it copies: where reads, writes and the copier go, and how the move ends.
 */
import Arrow from './Arrow.astro';
import Figure from './Figure.astro';
---

<Figure
    caption="The server holds both stores until the copy ends. Nobody has to stop publishing."
    summary="During a storage move the server holds the old and the new store together. Reads and listings use the old store. Uploads and deletes go to the new store first, then to the old store, and the request fails if either fails. The copier walks the assets in order, checks the size and SHA-256 of each old blob, writes it to the new store, and saves its position every 500 assets. With no failures the move is done and the new store becomes the active storage. With failures the move is failed, the server keeps the old store, and the page lists each blob that failed. The old store is never changed or deleted by the move."
>
    <ul class="routes">
        <li class="route">
            <p class="who">Reads and listings</p>
            <Arrow/>
            <div class="targets">
                <span class="dg-node store">Old store</span>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="route">
            <p class="who">Uploads and deletes</p>
            <Arrow/>
            <div class="targets">
                <span class="dg-node store store-new"><span class="order">1</span> New store</span>
                <span class="dg-node store"><span class="order">2</span> Old store</span>
                <p class="dg-note">If either fails, the request fails.</p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="route">
            <p class="who">The copier</p>
            <Arrow/>
            <div class="targets">
                <span class="dg-node store">Old store</span>
                <Arrow/>
                <span class="dg-node store store-new">New store</span>
                <p class="dg-note">Asset by asset, in order. Checks size and SHA-256. Saves its place every 500 assets.</p>
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="ends">
        <div class="end">
            <p><span class="dg-stamp dg-stamp-ok">done</span></p>
            <p>No failures. The new store becomes the active storage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="end">
            <p><span class="dg-stamp dg-stamp-bad">failed</span></p>
            <p>"N blobs could not be copied". The server keeps the old store and lists each failed blob.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Figure>

<style>
    .routes {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.875rem;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
    }

    .route {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 10rem 1.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 0.75rem;
        align-items: center;
    }

    .who {
        color: var(--tr-heading);
        font-weight: 650;
    }

    .targets {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.5rem 0.625rem;
    }

    .store {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.375rem;
        padding-block: 0.375rem;
        white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .store-new {
        background-color: var(--tr-accent-low);
        color: var(--tr-heading);
    }

    .order {
        display: inline-grid;
        place-items: center;
        width: 1.125rem;
        height: 1.125rem;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background-color: var(--tr-ticket);
        color: var(--tr-ticket-ink);
        font-size: 0.6875rem;
        font-weight: 750;
    }

    .targets .dg-note {
        flex-basis: 100%;
    }

    .ends {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-top: 1.25rem;
        padding-top: 1.25rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--tr-line);
    }

    .end {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
        gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    @container (max-width: 34rem) {
        .route {
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
            gap: 0.375rem;
        }

        .route > :global(.dg-arrow) {
            display: none;
        }

        .ends {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
    }
</style>
